.TH PHX-SERVICES 1 "2026-09-05" "Phalanx Duel" "Phalanx Duel Local Tooling"
.SH NAME
phx-services \- manage host-native Phalanx Duel services
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bin/services
.I command
.RI [ service | all ]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bin/services
controls the server, client, admin, site, and backlog services. Runtime state
is stored under
.B .phx/
and the tmux session is named
.B phx.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B start, stop, restart
Change service lifecycle state.
.TP
.B reload
Send SIGHUP to the server.
.TP
.B status
Show service state.
.TP
.B logs
Follow a daemonized service log.
.TP
.B attach
Attach to the phx tmux session.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -d, --daemon
Run in the background with logs under .phx/logs/.
.TP
.B -t, --tmux
Run in the detached phx tmux session.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show usage and exit successfully.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR phx-demo (1),
.BR phx (1),
.BR phx-dock (1)
